[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Module contains queries with a UML model as receiver.
This includes queries for retrieving model metadata
(acronym, title, version, URI, language), navigating
the model structure (main package, all classes, all
data types, all packages), and property file access.

Note: The main package is the top-level package of the
model as specified by the property MAIN_PACKAGE_NAME.
All generation targets operate on the main package
rather than the model root directly.

Note: Model metadata is resolved in order of priority:
(1) property file value, (2) ModelIdentification data
type in the model, (3) built-in fallback value.
This allows property file values to override model
metadata without modifying the model.

Related modules:
- packageQuery: queries with a UML package as receiver,
  since Model is a subtype of Package in UML
- classQuery: queries with a UML class as receiver
- dataTypeQuery: queries with a UML data type as receiver
/]
[module modelQuery(
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard'
)/]

[import ucmism2t::services::PropertiesService /]

[**
Returns the package identified by the main package name specified by
the property MAIN_PACKAGE_NAME. Returns the model itself if
MAIN_PACKAGE_NAME is not specified, is empty, matches the model name,
or is not found within the model. A uml::Model is a subtype of
uml::Package in the UML metamodel, so returning aModel as a
uml::Package is always valid.
---
AQL operations used:
  'MAIN_PACKAGE_NAME'.getPropertyValue() - Returns the value of the
                                           Acceleo generation property
                                           named MAIN_PACKAGE_NAME as
                                           a String. Returns empty
                                           string if the property is
                                           not set.
  aModel.eAllContents(uml::Package)      - Returns all uml::Package
                                           instances transitively
                                           contained in aModel,
                                           covering nested
                                           sub-packages at any depth.
  ->select(p | p.qualifiedName           - Filters to the package
    = propertyValue)                       whose qualified name
                                           matches the property value.
                                           Uses qualifiedName rather
                                           than name to uniquely
                                           identify the package in
                                           models with non-unique
                                           simple names.
  ->isEmpty()                            - Returns true if no package
                                           matched the property value.
  ->first()                              - Returns the first matching
                                           package. If qualifiedNames
                                           are unique, exactly one
                                           match is expected.

@param aModel - The root UML model used as the search scope.
/]
[query public u_mainPackage(aModel : uml::Model) : uml::Package =
  let propertyValue : String =
    'MAIN_PACKAGE_NAME'.getPropertyValue()
  let matchedPackages : OrderedSet(uml::Package) =
    aModel.eAllContents(uml::Package)
      ->select(p | p.qualifiedName = propertyValue)
  in
    if propertyValue = ''
      or propertyValue = aModel.name
      or matchedPackages->isEmpty()
    then
      aModel
    else
      matchedPackages->first()
    endif
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of all abstraction supplier classes and data
types in the model, sorted by name. Collects all abstraction
dependencies in the model, gathers their suppliers, and retains only
those that are exactly classes or data types.

@param aModel - A UML model whose abstraction supplier classes and
                data types are to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_abstractionSupplierClassifiers(
  aModel : uml::Model) : OrderedSet(uml::Classifier) =
  aModel.eAllContents(uml::Abstraction)
    ->collect(a | a.supplier)
    ->select(e | e.oclIsTypeOf(uml::Class) or e.oclIsKindOf(uml::DataType))
    ->asOrderedSet()
/]

